utral: agent started, context loaded, tool called, subagent spawned, subagent completed, artifact written, agent completed, run failed.\\n   - Avoid research-specific event types in the kernel.\\n\\n3. **Keep research semantics in the app.**\\n   - The app should own \`research-memory/\` layout, scout/report-writer definitions, source-note loading, and report artifact conventions.\\n   - The kernel should only know how to run agents, assemble context, manage subagents, emit protocol events, and expose traces.\\n\\n4. **Make filesystem agent definitions part of the demo story.**\\n   - Show that agents are defined by catalog files such as \`agent.md\` and optional context sidecars.\\n   - Show that context loaders are declared by agents and resolved through the loader catalog.\\n\\n5. **Preserve failure honesty.**\\n   - If the live model/tool loop cannot run, surface the missing prerequisite clearly.\\n   - Do not synthesize fake scout reports or fake traces.\\n\\n6. **Defer larger research features.**\\n   - External web search, source ranking, citations, richer UI design, and production retrieval can come later.\\n   - The base demo should first prove that the Agent Kernel can orchestrate nested agents and make their work inspectable without collapsing the kernel/app boundary.","block_type":"text"},"spanId":null,"parentEventId":null,"timestamp":"2026-07-02T21:31:35.834Z"}",
